ent-ClothingShoesLeatherBoots = leather boots
    .desc = Sturdy boots stitched together from tanned leather. They leak a little.

ent-ClothingShoesShortBoots = short boots
    .desc = Low leather boots that are easy to pull on before a journey.

ent-ClothingShoesBlackboots = dark boots
    .desc = A pair of dark, well-cobbled boots. You have a feeling they're in your size.

ent-ClothingShoesFurlinedboots = fur lined boots
    .desc = Leather boots, lined-and-cuffed with the fur of a forest-dwelling beaste.

ent-ClothingShoesSoldierboots = iron maille boots
    .desc = A pair of leather boots, reinforced with smaller iron plates along the feet and ankles. A thick layer of chainmail has been woven across the cuffs of each boot, and tastefully riveted into place. Colloquially known as 'soldier's boots', due to its widespread usage amongst Psydonia's oft-conscripted levies.

ent-ClothingShoesNobleboots = noble boots
    .desc = Fine dark leather boots.

ent-ClothingShoesAncientboots = decrepit boots
    .desc = Rotted metal greaves, shingled atop boots of rotted leather. The toebones of its former legionnaire remain within, rattling about with every step taken.

ent-ClothingShoesBronzegreaves = bronze greaves
    .desc = Padded sabatons of bronze, tightly strapped together and padded with hide from a fearsome beaste. The sandals clack about, yet they do not feel obstructive; if anything, you've never felt more agile while beplated.

ent-ClothingShoesPlateBoots = plated boots
    .desc = Custom-fitted sabatons, made from a series of interlinking steel plates. The only weakness it has, beyond its inaffordability amongst those of ignobility, is its inability to properly stand firm across softer surfaces. There's a very good reason as to why you'd rarely see a knight treading the Terrorbog's muddied paths, after all.
